=== SIGNATURE ===
expand_rng(ad_or_rng, [r_down], [c_right], [r_up], [c_left])

=== COMMENT ===
Grow or shrink an address or range and return it as a range string. r_down / c_right / r_up / c_left move the bottom / right / top / left edge outward by that many rows or cols (default 0); a NEGATIVE number pulls that edge inward. Clamps at row 1 / col 1. Format mirrors the input (A1 or numeric). A 1x1 result is a single address (no colon); a dimension of 0 or less, an array input or a non-integer returns #VALUE!.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(ad_or_rng, [r_down], [c_right], [r_up], [c_left],
  LET(
    grow_down, IF(ISOMITTED(r_down), 0, r_down),
    grow_right, IF(ISOMITTED(c_right), 0, c_right),
    grow_up, IF(ISOMITTED(r_up), 0, r_up),
    grow_left, IF(ISOMITTED(c_left), 0, c_left),
    single, ROWS(ad_or_rng) * COLUMNS(ad_or_rng) = 1,
    ok_int, LAMBDA(x, IFERROR(AND(ISNUMBER(x), x = INT(x)), FALSE)),
    args_ok, AND(ok_int(grow_down), ok_int(grow_right), ok_int(grow_up), ok_int(grow_left)),
    box, IFERROR(z_ad_box(ad_or_rng), 0),
    IF(OR(NOT(single), NOT(args_ok), COUNT(box) <> 4), #VALUE!,
      LET(
        top, MAX(1, SUM(INDEX(box, 1)) - grow_up),
        lft, MAX(1, SUM(INDEX(box, 2)) - grow_left),
        bot, MIN(1048576, SUM(INDEX(box, 3)) + grow_down),
        rgt, MIN(16384, SUM(INDEX(box, 4)) + grow_right),
        num_fmt, OR(ISNUMBER(ad_or_rng), AND(ISTEXT(ad_or_rng), NOT(REGEXTEST(ad_or_rng, "[A-Za-z]")))),
        corner_tl, IF(num_fmt, 1000000 * top + lft, ADDRESS(top, lft, 4)),
        corner_br, IF(num_fmt, 1000000 * bot + rgt, ADDRESS(bot, rgt, 4)),
        IF(OR(bot < top, rgt < lft), #VALUE!,
          IF(AND(bot = top, rgt = lft), corner_tl, corner_tl & ":" & corner_br))))
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Grow or shrink an address or range, working purely on coordinates - it never reads or cares about the cell contents.

Starting from the box of ad_or_rng, each optional moves one edge: r_down moves the bottom edge, c_right the right edge, r_up the top edge, c_left the left edge. A positive number moves that edge OUTWARD (the range grows); a negative number moves it INWARD (the range shrinks), so r_down = 2 adds two rows at the bottom and r_down = -2 removes the bottom two rows. Any edge pushed past the sheet is clamped to row 1 or column 1.

The result mirrors the input's format: an A1 input gives A1 ("F10:M12"); a numeric input gives numeric ("1000001:4000002"). A range is returned as "top-left:bottom-right". When the result is exactly one cell - whether by shrinking or because a single address was passed with nothing to do - it is returned as that single address with no colon: "B3" for A1 input, the numeric address (a number, e.g. 3000004) for numeric input. If a shrink leaves 0 or fewer rows or columns the result is #VALUE!.

ad_or_rng must be a single value of any of the four supported address/range types; an array returns #VALUE!. Each optional must be an integer (positive, zero or negative), or the result is #VALUE!.

Arguments:
  ad_or_rng - a single numeric address, A1 string, A1 range, or numeric range.
  [r_down]  - rows to add below (negative removes from the bottom)   (default 0).
  [c_right] - columns to add right (negative removes from the right)  (default 0).
  [r_up]    - rows to add above (negative removes from the top)       (default 0).
  [c_left]  - columns to add left (negative removes from the left)    (default 0).

Returns:
  A range string covering the resulting rectangle, in the input's format; a single address (no colon) when the result is one cell. #VALUE! for an array input, a non-integer optional, or a shrink that leaves no rows or columns.

Example:
  expand_rng("J10:K11", 1, 2, 0, 4)  ->  "F10:M12"
  expand_rng("B3", 0, 0, 10, 0)       ->  "B1:B3"
  expand_rng("B3", 0, 0, 0, 10)       ->  "A3:B3"
  expand_rng("B2:D6", -2)             ->  "B2:D4"     (two rows off the bottom)
  expand_rng("B2:D6", 0, -1, -1, 0)   ->  "B3:C6"     (one row off the top, one column off the right)
  expand_rng("B2:B3", -1)             ->  "B2"        (shrunk to one cell -> single address)
  expand_rng("B2:D6", -5)             ->  #VALUE!     (no rows left)
